{"id": "85846", "name": "משוואה ריבועית מבעיה מילולית – מידות מלבן לפי שטח, סעיפים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>A rectangle has length {{CT:0}}cm greater than its width. If it has an area of \\({{CT:1}}cm^2\\), find the dimensions of the rectangle.</p>\n <p>1. Write down an equation which relates the side lengths to the area of the rectangle. <br />[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:eq]]</p>\n <p>2. Solve your equation. Enter your answer as a set of numbers. <br /> [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:sol]]</p>\n <p>3. Hence, find the length of the shorter side. <br />[[input:ans3]] cm [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:short]]</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>If \\(x\\)cm is the width then \\((x+{{CT:2}})\\) is the length. Now the area is \\({{CT:1}}cm^2\\) and so \\[ {{CT:3}}.\\] \\[ {{CT:4}}=0\\] \\[ {{CT:5}} \\] So that \\(x={{CT:6}}\\) or \\(x={{CT:7}}\\). Since lengths are positive quantities \\(x&gt;0\\) and we discard the negative root. Hence the length of the shorter side is \\(x={{CT:7}}\\)cm.</p>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 1, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 1, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "ty